{% comment %}
  Free shipping progress.

  Renders nothing when the threshold is 0 or the cart is empty, so the merchant
  can switch it off from Theme settings → Cart without touching code.

  No JavaScript. The bar's width is correct in the server-rendered HTML, which
  is what the safety contract in CLAUDE.md requires — nothing here is hidden
  waiting for a script to reveal it.

  It stays in sync for free, but only if it is rendered inside a container the
  theme re-renders on cart change. Those are exactly two:

  - cart drawer  → anything inside `.drawer__inner`  (see cart-drawer.js:131)
  - cart page    → anything inside `.js-contents`    (see cart.js:164)

  Rendering it anywhere else on those pages will leave it showing a stale total.

  Accepts: nothing. Reads `cart` and `settings` directly.

  Usage:
  {% render 'shipping-progress' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign threshold = settings.free_shipping_threshold | times: 100
-%}

{%- if threshold > 0 and cart.item_count > 0 -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign remaining = threshold | minus: cart.total_price
    if remaining > 0
      assign percent = cart.total_price | times: 100 | divided_by: threshold
    else
      assign percent = 100
    endif
  -%}

  <div class="shipping-progress">
    <p class="shipping-progress__text label">
      {%- if remaining > 0 -%}
        Spend {{ remaining | money }} more for free shipping
      {%- else -%}
        Free shipping unlocked
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>

    <div class="shipping-progress__track" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="shipping-progress__fill" style="width: {{ percent }}%"></span>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
